{%- comment -%}
  NEGATIVE CONTROL handler — vuln_privesc. Represents a privileged admin effect. Because
  the manifest points at the member policy, a plain user reaches this handler → privilege
  escalation. The "effect" here is inert (returns a marker), but succeeding AT ALL as a
  user principal is the vulnerability.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign out = {}
  assign out['ok'] = true
  assign result = {}
  assign result['admin_action'] = 'rotate_all_tokens'
  assign result['executed_by'] = principal.id
  assign result['note'] = 'admin-only effect executed by a non-admin — privilege escalation'
  assign out['result'] = result
  return out
%}
